## 4. Data Input Methods

### File & Directory Monitoring
```ini
# inputs.conf
[monitor:///var/log/syslog]
disabled = false
sourcetype = syslog
index = os_logs

[monitor:///var/log/apache2/access.log]
disabled = false
sourcetype = access_combined
index = web_logs
```

### Network Inputs (TCP/UDP)
```ini
# inputs.conf — receive syslog on UDP 514
[udp://514]
sourcetype = syslog
index = network_logs

# TCP input on port 5514
[tcp://5514]
sourcetype = custom_tcp
index = custom_index
```

### Scripted Inputs
```ini
# inputs.conf — run a script every 60 seconds
[script:///opt/splunk/etc/apps/myapp/bin/my_script.sh]
interval = 60
sourcetype = custom_script
index = script_data
```

### HTTP Event Collector (HEC)
HEC allows sending data to Splunk over HTTP/HTTPS using tokens.

**Enable HEC in Splunk Web**: Settings → Data Inputs → HTTP Event Collector → Enable

```bash
# Send data via HEC using curl
curl -k https://<splunk_host>:8088/services/collector/event \
  -H "Authorization: Splunk <HEC_TOKEN>" \
  -d '{"event": "Hello from HEC", "sourcetype": "manual", "index": "main"}'
```

### Windows-Specific Inputs
```ini
# inputs.conf
[WinEventLog://Security]
disabled = false
index = win_security

[WinEventLog://Application]
disabled = false
index = win_app

[perfmon://CPU]
object = Processor
counters = % Processor Time
instances = _Total
interval = 30
index = perfmon
```

### Database Inputs (DB Connect)
Splunk DB Connect app allows pulling data from relational databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server) on a schedule.

