## 7. Field Extractions

### Automatic Extraction
Splunk automatically extracts fields like `host`, `source`, `sourcetype`, `_time`, `_raw` for every event. It also auto-extracts key=value pairs.

### Inline Extraction (Search-Time)
```spl
| rex field=_raw "user=(?<username>\w+)"
| rex field=_raw "duration=(?<duration>\d+\.?\d*)"
```

### Persistent Field Extraction (props.conf / transforms.conf)
```ini
# props.conf
[my_sourcetype]
EXTRACT-username = user=(?<username>\w+)
EXTRACT-duration = duration=(?<duration>\d+\.?\d*)

# For complex/reusable extractions, use transforms.conf
REPORT-myfields = my_transform_name
```
```ini
# transforms.conf
[my_transform_name]
REGEX = user=(?<username>\w+)\s+action=(?<action>\w+)
```

### Field Extraction via UI
**Settings → Fields → Field Extractions → New Field Extraction**
Use the interactive field extractor (IFX) for regex or delimiter-based extraction.

### Calculated Fields
```ini
# props.conf
[access_combined]
EVAL-response_sec = response_time / 1000
EVAL-status_type = if(status >= 400, "error", "ok")
```

### Field Aliases
```ini
# props.conf
[my_sourcetype]
FIELDALIAS-src = src_ip AS source_ip
FIELDALIAS-dest = dest_ip AS destination_ip
```

