## 14. Clustering

### Indexer Clustering
Indexer clusters provide data replication and high availability.

**Key Concepts:**
- **Replication Factor (RF)**: Number of copies of raw data (default: 3)
- **Search Factor (SF)**: Number of searchable copies (default: 2)
- **Cluster Master / Manager Node**: Coordinates the cluster

```ini
# server.conf on Manager Node
[clustering]
mode = manager
replication_factor = 3
search_factor = 2

# server.conf on Peer Nodes
[clustering]
mode = peer
manager_uri = https://<manager_ip>:8089

# server.conf on Search Head
[clustering]
mode = searchhead
manager_uri = https://<manager_ip>:8089
```

### Search Head Clustering (SHC)
Multiple search heads share configurations and load-balance searches.

**Components:**
- **Search Head Captain**: Elected leader that coordinates the cluster
- **Deployer**: Pushes apps and configurations to SHC members

```ini
# server.conf on SHC members
[shclustering]
conf_deploy_fetch_url = https://<deployer_ip>:8089
mgmt_uri = https://<this_SH_ip>:8089
replication_port = 9887
```

