## 15. Splunk REST API

Splunk exposes a REST API on port 8089 for programmatic access.

### Authentication
```bash
# Get a session token
curl -k -u admin:password https://localhost:8089/services/auth/login \
  -d username=admin -d password=changeme

# Use the token
curl -k -H "Authorization: Splunk <session_key>" \
  https://localhost:8089/services/search/jobs
```

### Common Endpoints
| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |
|----------|--------|---------|
| `/services/auth/login` | POST | Authenticate and get session key |
| `/services/search/jobs` | POST | Create a search job |
| `/services/search/jobs/<sid>` | GET | Get search job status |
| `/services/search/jobs/<sid>/results` | GET | Get search results |
| `/services/data/indexes` | GET | List indexes |
| `/services/data/inputs/monitor` | GET/POST | Manage file monitor inputs |
| `/services/server/info` | GET | Server information |
| `/services/apps/local` | GET | List installed apps |
| `/services/saved/searches` | GET/POST | Manage saved searches |

### Python SDK
```python
import splunklib.client as client
import splunklib.results as results

# Connect
service = client.connect(
    host="localhost",
    port=8089,
    username="admin",
    password="changeme"
)

# Run a search
search_query = "search index=main | head 10"
job = service.jobs.create(search_query)

# Wait for results
while not job.is_done():
    pass

# Read results
reader = results.JSONResultsReader(job.results(output_mode="json"))
for result in reader:
    if isinstance(result, dict):
        print(result)
```

