## 27. Key Formulas & Calculations to Remember

### Capacity Planning
```
Daily Storage = Daily Ingest Volume × Compression Factor × Replication Factor
Compression Factor ≈ 0.15 (Splunk compresses to ~15% of raw size)

Example: 100 GB/day, RF=3
Storage per day = 100 × 0.15 × 3 = 45 GB/day
30-day retention = 45 × 30 = 1,350 GB = 1.35 TB
```

### License Size Estimation
```
License Needed = Sum of all daily data ingested (before compression)
Includes data from all forwarders, HEC, scripted inputs, etc.
Does NOT count internal indexes (_internal, _audit)
```

### Search Concurrency
```
Max concurrent searches = Number of search heads × max_searches_per_cpu × CPUs
Default max_searches_per_cpu = 1 (configurable in limits.conf)
```

### Bucket Size Formula
```
Default hot bucket max size = auto ≈ 750 MB
Max warm buckets per index = 300 (default)
Max total index size = maxTotalDataSizeMB (default: 500 GB)
```

